          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 1244938,
            "text": "{\"data\":{\"extensionRegistry\":{\"extensions\":{\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjo3Nn0=\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/git-extras\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/git-extras\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/main/client/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"*\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Code analysis\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"commitlint\\\": {\\n    \\\"extends\\\": [\\n      \\\"@commitlint/config-conventional\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"actions\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"actionItem\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"${(config.git.blame.decorations === 'line' \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 'Show Git blame line annotations for the whole file') || (config.git.blame.decorations === 'file' \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 'Hide Git blame line annotations') || 'Show Git blame line annotations on selected lines'}\\\",\\n          \\\"iconURL\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-git-extras/63dd95962c43b95b3f3a9ea2aa0165d6b38a958c/icon/git_logo.svg?sanitize=true\\\",\\n          \\\"label\\\": \\\"Blame\\\",\\n          \\\"pressed\\\": \\\"(config.git.blame.decorations === 'line') || (config.git.blame.decorations === 'file')\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"Git\\\",\\n        \\\"command\\\": \\\"updateConfiguration\\\",\\n        \\\"commandArguments\\\": [\\n          [\\n            \\\"git.blame.decorations\\\"\\n          ],\\n          \\\"${(config.git.blame.decorations === 'line' \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 'file') || (config.git.blame.decorations === 'file' \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 'none') || 'line'}\\\",\\n          null\\n        ],\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"git.blame.toggle\\\",\\n        \\\"title\\\": \\\"${(config.git.blame.decorations === 'line' \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 'Show blame for the whole file') || (config.git.blame.decorations === 'file' \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 'Hide blame') || 'Show blame for selected lines'}\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"git.blame.decorations\\\": {\\n          \\\"default\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to decorate all lines in a file, only selected lines, or none at all.\\\",\\n          \\\"enum\\\": [\\n            \\\"none\\\",\\n            \\\"line\\\",\\n            \\\"file\\\"\\n          ],\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Git extras\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"menus\\\": {\\n      \\\"commandPalette\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"action\\\": \\\"git.blame.toggle\\\",\\n          \\\"when\\\": \\\"resource\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"editor/title\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"action\\\": \\\"git.blame.toggle\\\",\\n          \\\"when\\\": \\\"resource \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 clientApplication.isSourcegraph\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"date-fns\\\": \\\"^2.0.0-alpha.24\\\",\\n    \\\"rxjs\\\": \\\"^6.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"tagged-template-noop\\\": \\\"^2.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"A Sourcegraph extension that adds useful features when viewing files in a Git repository on Sourcegraph, GitHub, GitLab, and other supported code hosts.\\\",\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@commitlint/cli\\\": \\\"^11.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@commitlint/config-conventional\\\": \\\"^11.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@sourcegraph/prettierrc\\\": \\\"^2.2.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@sourcegraph/tsconfig\\\": \\\"^4.0.1\\\",\\n    \\\"@sourcegraph/tslint-config\\\": \\\"^13.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/expect\\\": \\\"1.20.4\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/lodash\\\": \\\"4.14.165\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/mocha\\\": \\\"5.2.7\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/node\\\": \\\"13.13.5\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/sinon\\\": \\\"7.0.13\\\",\\n    \\\"expect\\\": \\\"^24.1.0\\\",\\n    \\\"husky\\\": \\\"^1.3.1\\\",\\n    \\\"lnfs-cli\\\": \\\"^2.1.0\\\",\\n    \\\"lodash\\\": \\\"^4.17.11\\\",\\n    \\\"mkdirp\\\": \\\"^0.5.1\\\",\\n    \\\"mocha\\\": \\\"^6.1.4\\\",\\n    \\\"nyc\\\": \\\"^13.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"parcel-bundler\\\": \\\"^1.12.4\\\",\\n    \\\"prettier\\\": \\\"^1.19.1\\\",\\n    \\\"sinon\\\": \\\"^7.3.2\\\",\\n    \\\"source-map-support\\\": \\\"^0.5.12\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph\\\": \\\"^24.7.0\\\",\\n    \\\"ts-node\\\": \\\"^8.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"tslint\\\": \\\"^5.11.0\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"^3.9.3\\\",\\n    \\\"vscode-languageserver-types\\\": \\\"^3.14.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/git-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"husky\\\": {\\n    \\\"hooks\\\": {\\n      \\\"commit-msg\\\": \\\"commitlint -e $HUSKY_GIT_PARAMS\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/sourcegraph-git-extras.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"git-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"nyc\\\": {\\n    \\\"exclude\\\": [\\n      \\\"**/*.test.ts?(x)\\\",\\n      \\\"src/util/stubs.ts\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"extension\\\": [\\n      \\\".tsx\\\",\\n      \\\".ts\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"include\\\": [\\n      \\\"src/**/*.ts?(x)\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# sourcegraph-git-extras\\\\n\\\\n[![build](https://travis-ci.org/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-git-extras.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-git-extras)\\\\n[![codecov](https://codecov.io/gh/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-git-extras/branch/master/graph/badge.svg?token=c3KpMf1MaY)](https://codecov.io/gh/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-git-extras)\\\\n[![code style: prettier](https://img.shields.io/badge/code_style-prettier-ff69b4.svg)](https://github.com/prettier/prettier)\\\\n\\\\nA [Sourcegraph extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/extensions) that adds useful features when viewing files in a Git repository on [Sourcegraph](https://sourcegraph.com), GitHub, GitLab, and other [supported code hosts](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/extensions):\\\\n\\\\n- **Git: Show/hide blame**: toggles Git blame annotations with each line's last commit, author, date, etc.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-git-extras)\\\\n\\\\n[**➕ Add to Sourcegraph**](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/git-extras)\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot from 2018-10-28 17-55-20](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/47624533-f3a1e800-dada-11e8-81d9-3d4bd67fc08a.png)\\\\n![screenshot from 2018-10-28 17-55-02](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/47624534-f3a1e800-dada-11e8-9c08-9ce307653b20.png)\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-git-extras.git\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"parcel build --no-minify --out-file sourcegraph-git-extras.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"cover\\\": \\\"TS_NODE_COMPILER_OPTIONS='{\\\\\\\"module\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"commonjs\\\\\\\"}' nyc --require ts-node/register --require source-map-support/register --all mocha --opts mocha.opts --timeout 10000\\\",\\n    \\\"prettier\\\": \\\"prettier '**/*.{js?(on),ts?(x),scss,yml,md}' --write --list-different\\\",\\n    \\\"prettier-check\\\": \\\"npm run prettier -- --write=false\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"npm run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file sourcegraph-git-extras.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn typecheck \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 yarn test \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 yarn build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"TS_NODE_COMPILER_OPTIONS='{\\\\\\\"module\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"commonjs\\\\\\\"}' mocha --require ts-node/register --require source-map-support/register --opts mocha.opts\\\",\\n    \\\"tslint\\\": \\\"tslint -c tslint.json -p tsconfig.json './src/*.ts?(x)' './*.ts?(x)'\\\",\\n    \\\"typecheck\\\": \\\"tsc -p .\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"blame\\\",\\n    \\\"github\\\",\\n    \\\"gitlab\\\",\\n    \\\"code host\\\",\\n    \\\"author\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Git extras\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9176-sourcegraph-git-extras.js?c6ztfhra5y8w--sourcegraph-git-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxMzB9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/python\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/python\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:python\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Python using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/python\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"python\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Python\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Python code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/python` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/python) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/python`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Python code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using python on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Python code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9179-sourcegraph-python.js?c6zthrg2yc3c--sourcegraph-python\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNjh9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/typescript\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/typescript\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:typescript\\\",\\n    \\\"onLanguage:javascript\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"actions\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"actionItem\\\": {\\n          \\\"label\\\": \\\"${config.typescript.showExternalReferences \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 \\\\\\\"Hide references from other repositories\\\\\\\" || \\\\\\\"Show references from other repositories\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"command\\\": \\\"updateConfiguration\\\",\\n        \\\"commandArguments\\\": [\\n          [\\n            \\\"typescript.showExternalReferences\\\"\\n          ],\\n          \\\"${!config.typescript.showExternalReferences}\\\",\\n          null,\\n          \\\"json\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"externalReferences.toggle\\\",\\n        \\\"title\\\": \\\"${config.typescript.showExternalReferences \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 \\\\\\\"Hide references from other repositories\\\\\\\" || \\\\\\\"Show references from other repositories\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.accessToken\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The access token for the language server to use to fetch files from the Sourcegraph API. The extension will create this token and save it in your settings automatically.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.diagnostics.enable\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to show compile errors on lines (Default: false)\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.langserver.log\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The log level to pass to the TypeScript language server. Logs will be forwarded to the browser console with the prefix [langserver].\\\",\\n          \\\"enum\\\": [\\n            false,\\n            \\\"log\\\",\\n            \\\"info\\\",\\n            \\\"warn\\\",\\n            \\\"error\\\"\\n          ]\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.maxExternalReferenceRepos\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The maximum number of dependent packages to look in when searching for external references for a symbol (defaults to 20).\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.npmrc\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Settings to be written into an npmrc in key/value format. Can be used to specify custom registries and tokens.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.progress\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to report progress while fetching sources, installing dependencies etc. (Default: true)\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.restartAfterDependencyInstallation\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to restart the language server after dependencies were installed (default true)\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.serverUrl\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The address of the WebSocket language server to connect to (e.g. ws://host:8080).\\\",\\n          \\\"format\\\": \\\"url\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.showExternalReferences\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether or not a second references provider for external references will be registered (defaults to false).\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.sourcegraphUrl\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The address of the Sourcegraph instance from the perspective of the TypeScript language server.\\\",\\n          \\\"format\\\": \\\"url\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"typescript.tsserver.log\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The log level to pass to tsserver. Logs will be forwarded to the browser console with the prefix [tsserver].\\\",\\n          \\\"enum\\\": [\\n            false,\\n            \\\"terse\\\",\\n            \\\"normal\\\",\\n            \\\"requestTime\\\",\\n            \\\"verbose\\\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Settings\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"menus\\\": {\\n      \\\"panel/toolbar\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"action\\\": \\\"externalReferences.toggle\\\",\\n          \\\"when\\\": \\\"panel.activeView.id == 'references'\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"TypeScript/JavaScript code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/typescript\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"typescript\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for TypeScript/JavaScript\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides TypeScript/JavaScript code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/typescript)\\\\n\\\\n![TypeScript code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/133014/63376874-a92c7900-c343-11e9-98bb-631016f1eff7.gif)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/typescript` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/typescript) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/typescript`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any TypeScript code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Language server\\\\n\\\\nThis extension communicates with a language server over WebSockets. On Sourcegraph.com, this extension is already configured. If you are running a\\\\nprivate Sourcegraph instance, you should run your own language server. The server is available as a Docker image `sourcegraph/lang-typescript` from Docker Hub.\\\\n\\\\n### 🔐 Secure deployment 🔐\\\\n\\\\nIf you have private code, we recommend deploying the language server behind an\\\\nauth proxy (such as the example below using HTTP basic authentication in NGINX), a firewall, or a VPN.\\\\n\\\\n### HTTP basic authentication\\\\n\\\\nYou can prevent unauthorized access to the language server by enforcing HTTP basic authentication in nginx, which comes with the sourcegraph/server image. At a high level, you'll create a secret then put it in both the nginx config and in your Sourcegraph global settings so that logged-in users are authenticated when their browser makes requests to the TypeScript language server.\\\\n\\\\nHere's how to set it up:\\\\n\\\\nCreate an `.htpasswd` file in the Sourcegraph config directory with one entry:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n$ htpasswd -c ~/.sourcegraph/config/.htpasswd langserveruser\\\\nNew password:\\\\nRe-type new password:\\\\nAdding password for user langserveruser\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nAdd a location directive the [nginx.conf](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/admin/nginx) that will route requests to the TypeScript language server:\\\\n\\\\n```nginx\\\\n...\\\\nhttp {\\\\n    ...\\\\n    server {\\\\n        ...\\\\n        location / {\\\\n            ...\\\\n        }\\\\n\\\\n        location /typescript {\\\\n            proxy_pass http://host.docker.internal:8080;\\\\n            proxy_http_version 1.1;\\\\n            proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\\\\n            proxy_set_header Connection \\\\\\\"Upgrade\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n            auth_basic \\\\\\\"basic authentication is required to access the language server\\\\\\\";\\\\n            auth_basic_user_file /etc/sourcegraph/.htpasswd;\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n- If you're running the quickstart on Linux, change `host.docker.internal` to the output of `ip addr show docker0 | grep -Po 'inet \\\\\\\\K[\\\\\\\\d.]+'`.\\\\n- If you're using [Kubernetes](#using-kubernetes) (e.g. [deploy-sourcegraph](https://github.com/sourcegraph/deploy-sourcegraph)), change `host.docker.internal` to `lang-typescript`.\\\\n\\\\nAdd these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n    ```json\\\\n    \\\\\\\"typescript.serverUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ws://langserveruser:PASSWORD@host.docker.internal:7080/typescript\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"typescript.sourcegraphUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"http://host.docker.internal:7080\\\\\\\",\\\\n    ```\\\\n\\\\nFill in the `PASSWORD` that you created above.\\\\n\\\\n- If you're running the quickstart on Linux, change `host.docker.internal` to the output of `ip addr show docker0 | grep -Po 'inet \\\\\\\\K[\\\\\\\\d.]+'`.\\\\n- If you're using [Kubernetes](#using-kubernetes) (e.g. [deploy-sourcegraph](https://github.com/sourcegraph/deploy-sourcegraph)):\\\\n  - `typescript.serverUrl` is the address of the TypeScript language server from the perspective of a user's browser (e.g. https://sourcegraph.example.com/typescript)\\\\n  - `typescript.sourcegraphUrl` is the address of the Sourcegraph instance from the perspective of the TypeScript language server (e.g. http://sourcegraph-frontend:30080)\\\\n\\\\nFinally, restart the sourcegraph/server container (or nginx deployment if deployed to Kubernetes) to pick up the configuration change.\\\\n\\\\nAfter deploying the language server, unauthenticated access to `http://localhost:7080/typescript` (or https://sourcegraph.example.com/typescript) should be blocked, but code intelligence should work when you're logged in.\\\\n\\\\nYou can always revoke the `PASSWORD` by deleting the `.htpasswd` file and restarting nginx.\\\\n\\\\n### Using Docker\\\\n\\\\n1. Run the Go language server:\\\\n\\\\n   ```sh\\\\n   docker run -p 8080:8080 sourcegraph/lang-typescript\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   You can verify it's up and running with [`ws`](https://github.com/hashrocket/ws) (run this from the same machine your browser is running on):\\\\n\\\\n   ```sh\\\\n   $ go get -u github.com/hashrocket/ws\\\\n   $ ws ws://localhost:8080\\\\n   \\\\u003e\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable this extension on your Sourcegraph https://sourcegraph.example.com/extensions/sourcegraph/typescript\\\\n\\\\n1. Add these to your Sourcegraph settings in https://sourcegraph.example.com/site-admin/global-settings and make sure the port matches either the Docker command or your Kubernetes config:\\\\n\\\\n   ```json\\\\n   \\\\\\\"typescript.serverUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ws://localhost:8080\\\\\\\"\\\\n   \\\\\\\"typescript.sourcegraphUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"http://host.docker.internal:7080\\\\\\\",\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   If you're running on Linux, change `go.sourcegraphUrl` to the IP given by:\\\\n\\\\n   ```bash\\\\n   ip addr show docker0 | grep -Po 'inet \\\\\\\\K[\\\\\\\\d.]+'\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\nNow visit a TypeScript file and you should see code intelligence!\\\\n\\\\n#### TLS in Docker\\\\n\\\\nTo enable the use of Websocket with SSL pass the key/certificate pair as environment variables to the docker container.\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\ndocker run -p 8080:8080 -e TLS_KEY=\\\\\\\"$(cat sourcegraph.example.com.key)\\\\\\\" -e TLS_CERT=\\\\\\\"$(cat sourcegraph.example.com.crt)\\\\\\\" sourcegraph/lang-typescript\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nTo reuse the self-signed certificate created by following the steps [here](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/admin/nginx#tls-https) add these parameters to the run command above:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n-e NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/home/node/sourcegraph.example.com.crt -v ~/.sourcegraph/config:/home/node\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe self signed certificate's `Common Name (CN)` should be the host name of your host. Also make sure you use Websocket with SSL in your Sourcegraph settings to connect to the language server:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n\\\\\\\"typescript.serverUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"wss://localhost:8080\\\\\\\"\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Authentication proxies and firewalls\\\\n\\\\nSome customers deploy Sourcegraph behind an authentication proxy or firewall. If you do this, we\\\\nrecommend deploying the language server behind the proxy so that it can issue requests directly to\\\\nSourcegraph without going through the proxy. (Otherwise, you will need to configure the language\\\\nserver to authenticate through your proxy.) Make sure you set `typescript.sourcegraphUrl` to the URL\\\\nthat the language server should use to reach Sourcegraph, which is likely different from the URL\\\\nthat end users use.\\\\n\\\\n### Using Kubernetes\\\\n\\\\nTo deploy the language server with Kubernetes, use a deployment like this:\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\\\nkind: Deployment\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  name: lang-typescript\\\\nspec:\\\\n  replicas: 4 # adjust as needed\\\\n  selector:\\\\n    matchLabels:\\\\n      app: lang-typescript\\\\n  template:\\\\n    metadata:\\\\n      labels:\\\\n        app: lang-typescript\\\\n    spec:\\\\n      containers:\\\\n        - name: lang-typescript\\\\n          image: sourcegraph/lang-typescript\\\\n          ports:\\\\n            - containerPort: 8080\\\\n              name: wss\\\\n          env:\\\\n            # TLS certificate and key to secure the WebSocket connection (optional)\\\\n            - name: TLS_CERT\\\\n              value: ... your TLS certificate ...\\\\n            - name: TLS_KEY\\\\n              value: ... your TLS key ...\\\\n          # Resources to provision for the server (adjust as needed)\\\\n          resources:\\\\n            limits:\\\\n              cpu: '4'\\\\n              memory: 5Gi\\\\n            requests:\\\\n              cpu: 500m\\\\n              memory: 2Gi\\\\n          # Probes the server periodically to see if it is healthy\\\\n          livenessProbe:\\\\n            initialDelaySeconds: 30\\\\n            tcpSocket:\\\\n              port: wss\\\\n            timeoutSeconds: 5\\\\n          readinessProbe:\\\\n            tcpSocket:\\\\n              port: wss\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nWith a corresponding service:\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\napiVersion: v1\\\\nkind: Service\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  labels:\\\\n    app: lang-typescript\\\\n    deploy: lang-typescript\\\\n  name: lang-typescript\\\\nspec:\\\\n  ports:\\\\n    - name: wss\\\\n      port: 443\\\\n      targetPort: wss\\\\n  selector:\\\\n    app: lang-typescript\\\\n  type: LoadBalancer\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### TLS\\\\n\\\\nTo enable TLS, set the `TLS_KEY` and `TLS_CERT` environment variables. TLS optional but **strongly recommended** for production deployments.\\\\n\\\\n#### Enabling Prometheus metrics\\\\n\\\\nThe server exposes metrics on port 6060 that can be scraped by Prometheus.\\\\n\\\\n#### Improving performance with an SSD\\\\n\\\\nTo improve performance of dependency installation, the server can be configured to use a mounted SSD at a given directory by setting the `CACHE_DIR` environment variable. The instructions for how to mount a SSD depend on your deployment environment.\\\\n\\\\n1. Add a volume for the mount path of the SSD:\\\\n\\\\n   ```diff\\\\n     spec:\\\\n   + volumes:\\\\n   +   - hostPath:\\\\n   +       path: /path/to/mounted/ssd\\\\n   +     name: cache-ssd\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   For example, Google Cloud Platform mounts the first SSD disk to `/mnt/disks/ssd0`.\\\\n\\\\n2. Add a volume mount to the container spec:\\\\n\\\\n   ```diff\\\\n     image: sourcegraph/lang-typescript\\\\n   + volumeMounts:\\\\n   +   - mountPath: /mnt/cache\\\\n   +     name: cache-ssd\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n3. Tell the language server to use the mount as the root for temporary directories:\\\\n\\\\n   ```diff\\\\n     env:\\\\n   +   - name: CACHE_DIR\\\\n   +     value: /mnt/cache\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n#### Improving performance with an npm registry proxy\\\\n\\\\nTo further speed up dependency installation, all npm registry requests can be proxied through a cache running on the same node.\\\\n\\\\nExample deployment for Kubernetes:\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\\\nkind: Deployment\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  name: npm-proxy\\\\nspec:\\\\n  minReadySeconds: 10\\\\n  replicas: 1\\\\n  revisionHistoryLimit: 10\\\\n  strategy:\\\\n    rollingUpdate:\\\\n      maxSurge: 1\\\\n      maxUnavailable: 1\\\\n    type: RollingUpdate\\\\n  template:\\\\n    metadata:\\\\n      labels:\\\\n        app: npm-proxy\\\\n    spec:\\\\n      containers:\\\\n        - image: sourcegraph/npm-proxy:latest\\\\n          name: npm-proxy\\\\n          ports:\\\\n            - containerPort: 8080\\\\n              name: http\\\\n          resources:\\\\n            limits:\\\\n              cpu: '1'\\\\n              memory: 1Gi\\\\n          volumeMounts:\\\\n            - mountPath: /cache\\\\n              name: npm-proxy-cache\\\\n      volumes:\\\\n        - name: npm-proxy-cache\\\\n          persistentVolumeClaim:\\\\n            claimName: npm-proxy\\\\n---\\\\napiVersion: v1\\\\nkind: PersistentVolumeClaim\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  annotations:\\\\n    volume.beta.kubernetes.io/storage-class: default\\\\n  name: npm-proxy\\\\nspec:\\\\n  accessModes:\\\\n    - ReadWriteOnce\\\\n  resources:\\\\n    requests:\\\\n      storage: 100Gi\\\\n---\\\\napiVersion: v1\\\\nkind: Service\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  labels:\\\\n    app: npm-proxy\\\\n  name: npm-proxy\\\\nspec:\\\\n  ports:\\\\n    - name: http\\\\n      port: 8080\\\\n      targetPort: http\\\\n  selector:\\\\n    app: npm-proxy\\\\n  type: ClusterIP\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThen define a `.yarnrc` as a config map that points to the proxy:\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\napiVersion: v1\\\\ndata:\\\\n  .yarnrc: |\\\\n    # THIS IS AN AUTOGENERATED FILE. DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE DIRECTLY.\\\\n    # yarn lockfile v1\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n    https-proxy \\\\\\\"http://npm-proxy:8080\\\\\\\"\\\\n    proxy \\\\\\\"http://npm-proxy:8080\\\\\\\"\\\\n    strict-ssl false\\\\nkind: ConfigMap\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  name: yarn-config\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nand mount it into the container:\\\\n\\\\n```diff\\\\n  name: lang-typescript\\\\n+ volumeMounts:\\\\n+  - mountPath: /yarn-config\\\\n+    name: yarn-config\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n```diff\\\\n  spec:\\\\n+   volumes:\\\\n+     - configMap:\\\\n+         name: yarn-config\\\\n+       name: yarn-config\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Support for dependencies on private packages and git repositories\\\\n\\\\nDependencies on private npm packages and private registries is supported by setting the `typescript.npmrc` setting.\\\\nIt contains the same key/value settings as your `.npmrc` file in your home folder, and therefor supports the same scoping to registries and package scopes.\\\\nSee https://docs.npmjs.com/misc/config#config-settings for more information on what is possible to configure in `.npmrc`.\\\\n\\\\nExample:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n\\\\\\\"typescript.npmrc\\\\\\\": {\\\\n  \\\\\\\"//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"asfdh21e-1234-asdn-123v-1234asdb2\\\\\\\"\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor dependencies on private git repositories, mount an SSH key into `~/.ssh`.\\\\n\\\\n## Viewing communication between the browser and language server\\\\n\\\\nThis extension communicates from your browser to the language server that you deployed over WebSockets. This means that when you're viewing a code file on Sourcegraph, you can open the browser developer tools and refresh the page to capture the WebSocket connection and view the messages being sent and received:\\\\n\\\\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1387653/53431623-c0e30000-39a5-11e9-963d-42260ca12de3.png)\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/typescript\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json dist/extension.map sourceRoot https://sourcegraph.com/github.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-typescript@$(git rev-parse HEAD)/-/raw/extension/src/\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o src/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"typescript\\\",\\n    \\\"javascript\\\",\\n    \\\"cross-repository\\\",\\n    \\\"language-server\\\",\\n    \\\"react\\\",\\n    \\\"jsx\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9199-sourcegraph-typescript.js?c6zthubm11g0--sourcegraph-typescript\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNjl9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/go\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/go\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:go\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"actions\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"actionItem\\\": {\\n          \\\"label\\\": \\\"${config.go.showExternalReferences \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 \\\\\\\"Hide references from other repositories\\\\\\\" || \\\\\\\"Show references from other repositories\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"command\\\": \\\"updateConfiguration\\\",\\n        \\\"commandArguments\\\": [\\n          [\\n            \\\"go.showExternalReferences\\\"\\n          ],\\n          \\\"${!config.go.showExternalReferences}\\\",\\n          null,\\n          \\\"json\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"externalReferences.toggle\\\",\\n        \\\"title\\\": \\\"${config.go.showExternalReferences \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 \\\\\\\"Hide references from other repositories\\\\\\\" || \\\\\\\"Show references from other repositories\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"go.accessToken\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The access token for the language server to use to fetch files from the Sourcegraph API. The extension will create this token and save it in your settings automatically.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"go.corsAnywhereURL\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Address of a cors-anywhere service. This will cause the extension to send GDDO requests to this service instead of directly to api.godoc.org. For example: https://cors-anywhere.sourcegraph.com/https://api.godoc.org/importersgithub.com/sourcegraph/go-lsp. This would not be necessary if godoc.org set CORS headers.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"go.gddoURL\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The address to Go Doc Dot Org or a proxy that speaks the same API (only used on Sourcegraph.com).\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"go.maxExternalReferenceRepos\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The maximum number of repositories to look in when searching for external references for a symbol (defaults to 20).\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"go.serverUrl\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The address of the WebSocket language server to connect to (e.g. ws://host:4389).\\\",\\n          \\\"format\\\": \\\"url\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"go.showExternalReferences\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether or not a second references provider for external references will be registered (defaults to false).\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"go.sourcegraphUrl\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The address of the Sourcegraph instance from the perspective of the Go language server.\\\",\\n          \\\"format\\\": \\\"url\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Settings\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"menus\\\": {\\n      \\\"panel/toolbar\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"action\\\": \\\"externalReferences.toggle\\\",\\n          \\\"when\\\": \\\"panel.activeView.id == 'references'\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Go code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/go\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"go\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Go\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Go code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/go)\\\\n\\\\n![Go code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1387653/49856504-ce281f80-fda4-11e8-933b-f8fc67c98daf.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/go` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/go) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/go`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Go code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Language server\\\\n\\\\nThis extension communicates with a language server over WebSockets. On Sourcegraph.com, this extension is already configured. If you are running a\\\\nprivate Sourcegraph instance, you should run your own language server. The server is available as a Docker image `sourcegraph/lang-go` from Docker Hub.\\\\n\\\\n### 🔐 Secure deployment 🔐\\\\n\\\\nIf you have private code, we recommend deploying the language server behind an\\\\nauth proxy (such as the example below using HTTP basic authentication in NGINX), a firewall, or a VPN.\\\\n\\\\n### HTTP basic authentication\\\\n\\\\nYou can prevent unauthorized access to the language server by enforcing HTTP basic authentication in nginx, which comes with the sourcegraph/server image. At a high level, you'll create a secret then put it in both the nginx config and in your Sourcegraph global settings so that logged-in users are authenticated when their browser makes requests to the Go language server.\\\\n\\\\nHere's how to set it up:\\\\n\\\\nCreate an `.htpasswd` file in the Sourcegraph config directory with one entry:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n$ htpasswd -c ~/.sourcegraph/config/.htpasswd langserveruser\\\\nNew password:\\\\nRe-type new password:\\\\nAdding password for user langserveruser\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nAdd a location directive the [nginx.conf](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/admin/nginx) that will route requests to the Go language server:\\\\n\\\\n```nginx\\\\n...\\\\nhttp {\\\\n    ...\\\\n    server {\\\\n        ...\\\\n        location / {\\\\n            ...\\\\n        }\\\\n\\\\n        location /go {\\\\n            proxy_pass http://host.docker.internal:4389;\\\\n            proxy_http_version 1.1;\\\\n            proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\\\\n            proxy_set_header Connection \\\\\\\"Upgrade\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n            auth_basic \\\\\\\"basic authentication is required to access the language server\\\\\\\";\\\\n            auth_basic_user_file /etc/sourcegraph/.htpasswd;\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n- If you're running the quickstart on Linux, change `host.docker.internal` to the output of `ip addr show docker0 | grep -Po 'inet \\\\\\\\K[\\\\\\\\d.]+'`.\\\\n- If you're using [Kubernetes](#using-kubernetes) (e.g. [deploy-sourcegraph](https://github.com/sourcegraph/deploy-sourcegraph)), change `host.docker.internal` to `lang-go`.\\\\n\\\\nAdd these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n  \\\\\\\"go.serverUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ws://langserveruser:PASSWORD@example.host.docker.internal:7080/go\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"go.sourcegraphUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"http://example.host.docker.internal:7080\\\\\\\",\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFill in the `PASSWORD` that you created above.\\\\n\\\\n- If you're running the quickstart on macOS, change `example.host.docker.internal` to `host.docker.internal`.\\\\n- If you're running the quickstart on Linux, change `example.host.docker.internal` to the output of `ip addr show docker0 | grep -Po 'inet \\\\\\\\K[\\\\\\\\d.]+'`.\\\\n- If you're using [Kubernetes](#using-kubernetes) (e.g. [deploy-sourcegraph](https://github.com/sourcegraph/deploy-sourcegraph)):\\\\n  - `go.serverUrl` is the address of the Go language server from the perspective of a user's browser (e.g. https://sourcegraph.example.com/go)\\\\n  - `go.sourcegraphUrl` is the address of the Sourcegraph instance from the perspective of the Go language server (e.g. http://sourcegraph-frontend:30080)\\\\n\\\\nFinally, restart the sourcegraph/server container (or nginx deployment if deployed to Kubernetes) to pick up the configuration change.\\\\n\\\\nAfter deploying the language server, unauthenticated access to `http://localhost:7080/go` (or https://sourcegraph.example.com/go) should be blocked, but code intelligence should work when you're logged in.\\\\n\\\\nYou can always revoke the `PASSWORD` by deleting the `.htpasswd` file and restarting nginx.\\\\n\\\\n### Using Docker\\\\n\\\\n1. Run the Go language server:\\\\n\\\\n   ```sh\\\\n   docker run --rm --name lang-go -p 4389:4389 sourcegraph/lang-go \\\\\\\\\\\\n     go-langserver -mode=websocket -addr=:4389 -usebuildserver -usebinarypkgcache=false -freeosmemory=false\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   You can verify it's up and running with [`ws`](https://github.com/hashrocket/ws) (run this from the same machine your browser is running on):\\\\n\\\\n   ```sh\\\\n   $ go get -u github.com/hashrocket/ws\\\\n   $ ws ws://localhost:4389\\\\n   \\\\u003e\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable this extension on your Sourcegraph https://sourcegraph.example.com/extensions/sourcegraph/go\\\\n\\\\n1. Add these to your Sourcegraph settings in https://sourcegraph.example.com/site-admin/global-settings and make sure the port matches either the Docker command or your Kubernetes config:\\\\n\\\\n   ```sh\\\\n   \\\\\\\"go.serverUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ws://localhost:4389\\\\\\\",\\\\n   \\\\\\\"go.sourcegraphUrl\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"http://host.docker.internal:7080\\\\\\\",\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   If you're running on Linux, change `go.sourcegraphUrl` to the IP given by:\\\\n\\\\n   ```bash\\\\n   ip addr show docker0 | grep -Po 'inet \\\\\\\\K[\\\\\\\\d.]+'\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\nNow visit a Go file and you should see code intelligence!\\\\n\\\\n### Using Kubernetes\\\\n\\\\nTo deploy the language server with Kubernetes, use a deployment like this:\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\napiVersion: extensions/v1beta1\\\\nkind: Deployment\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  annotations:\\\\n    description: Go code intelligence provided by lang-go\\\\n  name: lang-go\\\\n  namespace: prod\\\\nspec:\\\\n  minReadySeconds: 10\\\\n  replicas: 1\\\\n  revisionHistoryLimit: 10\\\\n  strategy:\\\\n    rollingUpdate:\\\\n      maxSurge: 1\\\\n      maxUnavailable: 1\\\\n    type: RollingUpdate\\\\n  template:\\\\n    metadata:\\\\n      labels:\\\\n        app: lang-go\\\\n    spec:\\\\n      containers:\\\\n        - args:\\\\n            - go-langserver\\\\n            - -mode=websocket\\\\n            - -addr=:4389\\\\n            - -usebuildserver\\\\n            - -usebinarypkgcache=false\\\\n            - -cachedir=$(CACHE_DIR)\\\\n            - -freeosmemory=false\\\\n          env:\\\\n            # TLS is optional\\\\n            - name: TLS_CERT\\\\n              valueFrom:\\\\n                secretKeyRef:\\\\n                  key: cert\\\\n                  name: tls\\\\n            - name: TLS_KEY\\\\n              valueFrom:\\\\n                secretKeyRef:\\\\n                  key: key\\\\n                  name: tls\\\\n            - name: POD_NAME\\\\n              valueFrom:\\\\n                fieldRef:\\\\n                  fieldPath: metadata.name\\\\n            - name: CACHE_DIR\\\\n              value: /mnt/cache/$(POD_NAME)\\\\n          image: sourcegraph/lang-go:latest\\\\n          livenessProbe:\\\\n            initialDelaySeconds: 5\\\\n            tcpSocket:\\\\n              port: lsp\\\\n            timeoutSeconds: 5\\\\n          name: lang-go\\\\n          ports:\\\\n            - containerPort: 4389\\\\n              name: lsp\\\\n            - containerPort: 6060\\\\n              name: debug\\\\n          readinessProbe:\\\\n            tcpSocket:\\\\n              port: 4389\\\\n          resources:\\\\n            limits:\\\\n              cpu: '8'\\\\n              memory: 10G\\\\n            requests:\\\\n              cpu: '1'\\\\n              memory: 10G\\\\n          volumeMounts:\\\\n            - mountPath: /mnt/cache\\\\n              name: cache-ssd\\\\n      volumes:\\\\n        - hostPath:\\\\n            path: /mnt/disks/ssd0/pod-tmp\\\\n          name: cache-ssd\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nWith a corresponding service:\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\napiVersion: v1\\\\nkind: Service\\\\nmetadata:\\\\n  annotations:\\\\n    prometheus.io/port: '6060'\\\\n    prometheus.io/scrape: 'true'\\\\n  labels:\\\\n    app: lang-go\\\\n  name: lang-go\\\\n  namespace: prod\\\\nspec:\\\\n  loadBalancerIP: your.static.ip.address\\\\n  ports:\\\\n    - name: debug\\\\n      port: 6060\\\\n      targetPort: debug\\\\n    - name: lsp\\\\n      port: 443\\\\n      targetPort: lsp\\\\n  selector:\\\\n    app: lang-go\\\\n  type: LoadBalancer\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n#### TLS\\\\n\\\\nTo enable TLS, set the `TLS_KEY` and `TLS_CERT` environment variables. TLS optional but **strongly recommended** for production deployments.\\\\n\\\\n#### Scaling out by increasing the replica count\\\\n\\\\nTo run multiple instances of the go-langserver and distribute connections between them in Kubernetes, set `spec.replicas` in the deployment YAML:\\\\n\\\\n```diff\\\\n spec:\\\\n   minReadySeconds: 10\\\\n-  replicas: 1\\\\n+  replicas: 5\\\\n   revisionHistoryLimit: 10\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Support for dependencies on private git repositories\\\\n\\\\n🚨 Before mounting your credentials into the language server, make sure the language server is hidden behind an auth proxy or firewall. 🚨\\\\n\\\\n### Private dependencies via `.netrc`\\\\n\\\\nMake sure your `$HOME/.netrc` contains:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nmachine codeload.github.com\\\\nlogin \\\\u003cyour username\\\\u003e\\\\npassword \\\\u003cyour password OR access token\\\\u003e\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nMount it into the container:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\ndocker run ... -v \\\\\\\"$HOME/.netrc\\\\\\\":/root/.netrc ...\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nVerify fetching works:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n$ docker exec -ti lang-go sh\\\\n# curl -n https://codeload.github.com/you/your-private-repo/zip/master\\\\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\\\\n...\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Private dependencies via SSH keys\\\\n\\\\nMake sure your `~/.gitconfig` contains these lines:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n[url \\\\\\\"git@github.com:\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    insteadOf = https://github.com/\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nMount that and your SSH keys into the container:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\ndocker run ... -v \\\\\\\"$HOME/.gitconfig\\\\\\\":/root/.gitconfig -v \\\\\\\"$HOME/.ssh\\\\\\\":/root/.ssh ...\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nVerify cloning works:\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n$ docker exec -ti lang-go sh\\\\n# git clone https://github.com/you/your-private-repo\\\\nCloning into 'your-private-repo'...\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Viewing communication between the browser and language server\\\\n\\\\nThis extension communicates from your browser to the language server that you deployed over WebSockets. This means that when you're viewing a code file on Sourcegraph, you can open the browser developer tools and refresh the page to capture the WebSocket connection and view the messages being sent and received:\\\\n\\\\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1387653/53431623-c0e30000-39a5-11e9-963d-42260ca12de3.png)\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/go\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json dist/extension.map sourceRoot https://sourcegraph.com/github.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph-go@$(git rev-parse HEAD)/-/raw/extension/src/\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o src/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"go\\\",\\n    \\\"cross-repository\\\",\\n    \\\"language-server\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9178-sourcegraph-go.js?c6zthr75n9qo--sourcegraph-go\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzF9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/cpp\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/cpp\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:cpp\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for C++ using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/cpp\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"cpp\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for C++\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides C++ code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/cpp` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/cpp) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/cpp`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any C++ code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using cpp on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"C++ code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9198-sourcegraph-cpp.js?c6zthu9grbgw--sourcegraph-cpp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzJ9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/r\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/r\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:r\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for R using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/r\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"r\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for R\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides R code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/r` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/r) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/r`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any R code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using r on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"R code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9183-sourcegraph-r.js?c6zthsiawwow--sourcegraph-r\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzN9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/java\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/java\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:java\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Java using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/java\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"java\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Java\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Java code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/java` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/java) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/java`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Java code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using java on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Java code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9197-sourcegraph-java.js?c6zthu8kgf9s--sourcegraph-java\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzR9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/ruby\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/ruby\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:ruby\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Ruby using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/ruby\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"ruby\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Ruby\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Ruby code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/ruby` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/ruby) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/ruby`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Ruby code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using ruby on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Ruby code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9177-sourcegraph-ruby.js?c6zthq88tpgo--sourcegraph-ruby\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzV9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/php\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/php\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:php\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for PHP using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/php\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"php\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for PHP\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides PHP code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/php` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/php) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/php`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any PHP code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using php on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"PHP code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9192-sourcegraph-php.js?c6zthtczy5ow--sourcegraph-php\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzZ9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/csharp\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/csharp\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:csharp\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for C# using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/csharp\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"csharp\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for C#\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides C# code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/csharp` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/csharp) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/csharp`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any C# code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using csharp on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"C# code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9206-sourcegraph-csharp.js?c6zthvg2tb9s--sourcegraph-csharp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzd9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/shell\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/shell\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:shell\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Shell using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/shell\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"shell\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Shell\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Shell code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/shell` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/shell) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/shell`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Shell code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using shell on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Shell code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9209-sourcegraph-shell.js?c6zthwd6gkq8--sourcegraph-shell\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzh9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/scala\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/scala\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:scala\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Scala using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/scala\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"scala\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Scala\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Scala code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/scala` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/scala) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/scala`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Scala code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using scala on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Scala code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9190-sourcegraph-scala.js?c6zthsykvoq8--sourcegraph-scala\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxNzl9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/swift\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/swift\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:swift\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Swift using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/swift\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"swift\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Swift\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Swift code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/swift` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/swift) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/swift`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Swift code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using swift on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Swift code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9182-sourcegraph-swift.js?c6zths1f5ffc--sourcegraph-swift\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODB9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/rust\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/rust\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:rust\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Rust using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/rust\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"rust\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Rust\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Rust code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/rust` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/rust) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/rust`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Rust code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using rust on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Rust code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9188-sourcegraph-rust.js?c6zthsw5lvsg--sourcegraph-rust\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODF9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/kotlin\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/kotlin\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:kotlin\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Kotlin using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/kotlin\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"kotlin\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Kotlin\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Kotlin code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/kotlin` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/kotlin) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/kotlin`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Kotlin code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using kotlin on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Kotlin code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9186-sourcegraph-kotlin.js?c6zthsq7t600--sourcegraph-kotlin\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODJ9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/elixir\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/elixir\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:elixir\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Elixir using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/elixir\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"elixir\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Elixir\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Elixir code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/elixir` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/elixir) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/elixir`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Elixir code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using elixir on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Elixir code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9201-sourcegraph-elixir.js?c6zthujs76tc--sourcegraph-elixir\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODN9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/perl\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/perl\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:perl\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Perl using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/perl\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"perl\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Perl\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Perl code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/perl` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/perl) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/perl`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Perl code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using perl on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Perl code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9193-sourcegraph-perl.js?c6zthtgvv70w--sourcegraph-perl\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODR9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/lua\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/lua\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:lua\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Lua using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/lua\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"lua\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Lua\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Lua code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/lua` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/lua) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/lua`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Lua code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using lua on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Lua code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9180-sourcegraph-lua.js?c6zthrwi77hs--sourcegraph-lua\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODV9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/clojure\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/clojure\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:clojure\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Clojure using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/clojure\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"clojure\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Clojure\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Clojure code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/clojure` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/clojure) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/clojure`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Clojure code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using clojure on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Clojure code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9196-sourcegraph-clojure.js?c6zthu0sd0yg--sourcegraph-clojure\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODZ9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/haskell\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/haskell\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:haskell\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Haskell using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/haskell\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"haskell\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Haskell\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Haskell code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/haskell` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/haskell) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/haskell`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Haskell code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using haskell on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Haskell code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9185-sourcegraph-haskell.js?c6zthsj9xtfs--sourcegraph-haskell\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODd9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/powershell\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/powershell\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:powershell\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for PowerShell using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/powershell\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"powershell\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for PowerShell\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides PowerShell code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/powershell` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/powershell) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/powershell`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any PowerShell code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using powershell on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"PowerShell code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9184-sourcegraph-powershell.js?c6zthsij36ts--sourcegraph-powershell\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODh9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/lisp\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/lisp\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:lisp\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Lisp using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/lisp\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"lisp\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Lisp\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Lisp code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/lisp` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/lisp) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/lisp`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Lisp code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using lisp on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Lisp code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9189-sourcegraph-lisp.js?c6zthsy9esj4--sourcegraph-lisp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoxODl9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/erlang\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/erlang\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:erlang\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Erlang using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/erlang\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"erlang\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Erlang\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Erlang code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/erlang` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/erlang) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/erlang`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Erlang code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using erlang on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": 