  \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for CUDA using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/cuda\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"cuda\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for CUDA\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides CUDA code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/cuda` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/cuda) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/cuda`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any CUDA code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using cuda on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"CUDA code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9202-sourcegraph-cuda.js?c6zthumezheo--sourcegraph-cuda\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyMzN9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/pascal\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/pascal\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:pascal\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Pascal using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/pascal\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"pascal\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Pascal\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Pascal code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/pascal` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/pascal) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/pascal`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Pascal code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using pascal on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Pascal code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9205-sourcegraph-pascal.js?c6zthuzb6qcg--sourcegraph-pascal\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyMzR9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/verilog\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/verilog\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:verilog\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Verilog using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/verilog\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"verilog\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Verilog\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Verilog code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/verilog` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/verilog) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/verilog`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Verilog code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using verilog on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Verilog code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9181-sourcegraph-verilog.js?c6zths18rwb4--sourcegraph-verilog\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyMzV9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/vhdl\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/vhdl\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:vhdl\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for VHDL using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/vhdl\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"vhdl\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for VHDL\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides VHDL code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/vhdl` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/vhdl) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/vhdl`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any VHDL code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using vhdl on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"VHDL code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9210-sourcegraph-vhdl.js?c6zthwsbfupk--sourcegraph-vhdl\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyMzZ9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/graphql\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/graphql\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:graphql\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for GraphQL using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/graphql\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"graphql\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for GraphQL\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides GraphQL code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/graphql` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/graphql) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/graphql`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any GraphQL code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using graphql on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"GraphQL code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9208-sourcegraph-graphql.js?c6zthvug6jrc--sourcegraph-graphql\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyMzd9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/groovy\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/groovy\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:groovy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Groovy using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/groovy\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"groovy\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Groovy\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Groovy code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/groovy` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/groovy) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/groovy`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Groovy code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using groovy on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Groovy code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9207-sourcegraph-groovy.js?c6zthvtvjvnc--sourcegraph-groovy\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyNDJ9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/protobuf\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/protobuf\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:protobuf\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Protocol Buffers using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/protobuf\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"protobuf\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Protocol Buffers\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Protocol Buffers code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/protobuf` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/protobuf) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/protobuf`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Protocol Buffers code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using protobuf on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Protocol Buffers code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9187-sourcegraph-protobuf.js?c6zthssfeaag--sourcegraph-protobuf\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyNDh9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/jsonnet\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/jsonnet\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:jsonnet\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Jsonnet using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/jsonnet\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"jsonnet\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Jsonnet\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Jsonnet code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/jsonnet` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/jsonnet) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/jsonnet`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Jsonnet code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using jsonnet on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Jsonnet code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9194-sourcegraph-jsonnet.js?c6zthtr69yq0--sourcegraph-jsonnet\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyNTB9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/thrift\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/thrift\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:thrift\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Thrift using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/thrift\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"thrift\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Thrift\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Thrift code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/thrift` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/thrift) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/thrift`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Thrift code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using thrift on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Thrift code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9191-sourcegraph-thrift.js?c6zthtcmk9p4--sourcegraph-thrift\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyNjB9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/cobol\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/cobol\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:cobol\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Cobol using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/cobol\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"cobol\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Cobol\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Cobol code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/cobol` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/cobol) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/cobol`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Cobol code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using cobol on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Cobol code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9200-sourcegraph-cobol.js?c6zthuf1buig--sourcegraph-cobol\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false},{\"id\":\"UmVnaXN0cnlFeHRlbnNpb246eyJsIjoyNjF9\",\"extensionID\":\"sourcegraph/tcl\",\"url\":\"/extensions/sourcegraph/tcl\",\"manifest\":{\"raw\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sourcegraph/sourcegraph/master/shared/src/schema/extension.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"activationEvents\\\": [\\n    \\\"onLanguage:tcl\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserslist\\\": [\\n    \\\"last 1 Chrome versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Firefox versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Edge versions\\\",\\n    \\\"last 1 Safari versions\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"categories\\\": [\\n    \\\"Programming languages\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"contributes\\\": {\\n    \\\"configuration\\\": {\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include archived repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to include forked repositories in search results.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use only indexed requests to the search API.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"The timeout (in milliseconds) for un-indexed search requests.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.disableRangeQueries\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to fetch multiple precise definitions and references on hover.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Whether to use pre-computed LSIF data for code intelligence (such as hovers, definitions, and references). See https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence.\\\",\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Basic code intelligence settings\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Provides basic code intelligence for Tcl using the Sourcegraph search API\\\",\\n  \\\"engines\\\": {\\n    \\\"node\\\": \\\"\\\\u003e=11.1.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"extensionID\\\": \\\"sourcegraph/tcl\\\",\\n  \\\"files\\\": [\\n    \\\"dist\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"icon\\\": \\\"data:image/png;base64,\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n  \\\"main\\\": \\\"dist/extension.js\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"tcl\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"publisher\\\": \\\"sourcegraph\\\",\\n  \\\"readme\\\": \\\"# Code intelligence for Tcl\\\\n\\\\nThis extension provides Tcl code intelligence on Sourcegraph.\\\\n\\\\n[**🗃️ Source code**](https://github.com/sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions/tree/master/extensions/template)\\\\n\\\\n![Python code intelligence](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882679-68768580-139a-11e9-8e58-a756c5bf4fb0.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Usage\\\\n\\\\n1. Enable the `sourcegraph/tcl` extension:\\\\n   - On Sourcegraph.com, visit the [extension page](https://sourcegraph.com/extensions/sourcegraph/tcl) to enable it.\\\\n   - On a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, select **User menu \\\\u003e Extensions**, search for `sourcegraph/tcl`, and enable it.\\\\n1. Visit any Tcl code file on Sourcegraph.\\\\n1. Hover over a token in the code file.\\\\n   - See a description of the token.\\\\n   - Click **Go to definition** (if available) to go to the token's definition.\\\\n   - Click **Find references** to see all references to the token.\\\\n\\\\n### On your code host\\\\n\\\\nThis extension adds the same features to code files and diffs on your code host if you're using the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension). To use it on your code host:\\\\n\\\\n1. Follow the [usage steps](#usage) above to enable this extension.\\\\n1. Install the [Sourcegraph browser extension](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/integration/browser_extension).\\\\n   - If you're using it with a self-hosted Sourcegraph instance, enter the Sourcegraph instance URL into the Sourcegraph browser extension options menu. Then click the gear icon and enable _Experimental features: Use extensions_.\\\\n1. Visit any file on your code host and hover over a token to see a description of the token, a **Go to definition** action (if available), and a **Find references** action.\\\\n\\\\n![screenshot of using tcl on GitHub](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1976/50882271-0c5f3180-1399-11e9-9697-e4e4fa4e29e9.png)\\\\n\\\\n## Basic code intelligence\\\\n\\\\nThis extension comes with built-in code intelligence provided by [search-based heuristics](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/basic_code_intelligence). Because this extension uses text-based heuristics, its definition and reference results are not precise:\\\\n\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Go to definition\\\\\\\" on a token goes to the definition found by [universal-ctags](https://github.com/universal-ctags/ctags), a cross-language parsing suite.\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Find references\\\\\\\" on a token finds all instances of token (with the same case) in the current repository and other repositories.\\\\n\\\\nThese heuristics work well for tokens with unique names, such as `render_to_view` or `TLSConfig`. They do not work well for ambiguous tokens, such as `open` or `file`.\\\\n\\\\n### Indexed and archived repositories\\\\n\\\\nTo include indexed and/or archived repositories in search results, add the following to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeForks\\\\\\\": true,\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.includeArchives\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Large repositories\\\\n\\\\nBasic code intelligence will perform a search query in the commit you are viewing. This may cause performance issues if the commit is not indexed and the repository is large. After a timeout period with no results, an index-only search will be performed. This type of query may return results for a commit other than the one you are currently viewing. The default timeout period is five seconds, but can be lowered by adding the following to your Sourcegraph global settings (units are milliseconds):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.unindexedSearchTimeout\\\\\\\": 1000\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nFor organizations that organize code in a monorepo, it may never be useful to perform an un-indexed search. To force only indexed search queries, add the following to your Sourcgraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"basicCodeIntel.indexOnly\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## LSIF\\\\n\\\\nTo enable [LSIF support](https://docs.sourcegraph.com/code_intelligence/explanations/precise_code_intelligence), add these to your Sourcegraph global settings:\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n  \\\\\\\"codeIntel.lsif\\\\\\\": true\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"repository\\\": {\\n    \\\"directory\\\": \\\"extensions/template\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"git\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"github:sourcegraph/code-intel-extensions\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/tsc -b . \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel build --out-file extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"config-types\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/dot-json package.json contributes.configuration | ../../node_modules/.bin/json2ts --unreachableDefinitions --style.singleQuote --no-style.semi -o ../../shared/search/settings.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"publish\\\": \\\"yarn -s \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 src -config \\\\\\\"${SRC_CONFIG}\\\\\\\" ext publish\\\",\\n    \\\"serve\\\": \\\"yarn run symlink-package \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/parcel serve --no-hmr --out-file dist/extension.js src/extension.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"sourcegraph:prepublish\\\": \\\"yarn run build\\\",\\n    \\\"symlink-package\\\": \\\"../../node_modules/.bin/mkdirp dist \\\\u0026\\\\u0026 ../../node_modules/.bin/lnfs ./package.json ./dist/package.json\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"sideEffects\\\": false,\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\n    \\\"fuzzy\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Tcl code intelligence\\\",\\n  \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://sourcegraph.com/-/static/extension/9211-sourcegraph-tcl.js?c6zthx68qlkw--sourcegraph-tcl\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.0.0-DEVELOPMENT\\\"\\n}\"},\"viewerCanAdminister\":false}]}}}}"
